#title: Finite planar fracture on a refined grid (0.005 m)
#num_threads: 48
#domain: 8.0 10.0 10.0
#dx_dy_dz: 0.005 0.005 0.005
#time_window: 250e-9

#material: 9.0 1e-4 1 0 rock
#material: 80.0 0.5 1 0 my_water

#waveform: ricker 100 100e6 my_ricker
#hertzian_dipole: z 0.5 5.0 5.5 my_ricker
#rx: 0.5 5.0 4.5

#box: 0 0 0 8.0 10.0 10.0 rock
#cylinder: 0.5 5.0 0 0.5 5.0 10.0 0.075 my_water

## The fracture of ../For_full-domain_verifications/3D8x10x10-shifted_frac-dist6-4h_planar_h0pt01.in,
## written as a box: the slab x in [6.48, 6.52] m, y and z in [1, 9] m, which is what that model's
## HDF5 volume holds. Its faces lie on cell faces at 0.01 m and at 0.005 m, so the aperture
## (0.04 m) and the extent (8 x 8 m) are the same on both grids. The fill is water
## (eps_r 80, sigma 0.5 S/m); averaging is off ("n"), as with #geometry_objects_read.
## A Hertzian dipole is one cell long in gprMax, so its moment halves with the cell: multiply
## the 0.005 m traces by 2 to compare them with the 0.01 m ones.
#box: 6.48 1.0 1.0 6.52 9.0 9.0 my_water n
